ics."},{"question":"How to interpret the Trade balance - Merchandise data?","answer":"A surplus trade balance typically strengthens a currency, while a deficit can weaken it.^Assess the trade balance in light of external sector indicators such as foreign exchange reserves, external debt, and capital flows to evaluate overall external sector stability.^Analyse how trade balance data influences monetary and fiscal policies, including exchange rate management, trade tariffs, and foreign investment regulations.^Consider global indicators such as commodity prices, trade barriers, and international economic growth forecasts to understand external factors impacting the trade balance.^Observe the reaction of financial markets, especially currency and stock markets, to changes in trade balance data, as it can affect investor sentiment and capital flows."}],"related":[{"slug":"10y-g-sec-yield","title":"10Y G-Sec Yield"},{"slug":"current-account-deficit-gdp","title":"Current Account Deficit (% GDP)"},{"slug":"gold-price","title":"Gold Price"},{"slug":"government-consumption-gfce","title":"Government Consumption (GFCE)"},{"slug":"gross-fixed-capital-formation-gfcf","title":"Gross Fixed Capital Formation (GFCF)"},{"slug":"gross-value-added-gva-agriculture","title":"Gross Value Added (GVA) - Agriculture"},{"slug":"gross-value-added-gva-financial-services-real-estate-and-business-services","title":"Gross Value Added (GVA) - Financial, Real Estate and Business Services"},{"slug":"gross-value-added-gva-industry","title":"Gross Value Added (GVA) - Industry"},{"slug":"gross-value-added-gva-overall","title":"Gross Value Added (GVA)- Overall"},{"slug":"gross-value-added-gva-services","title":"Gross Value Added (GVA) - Services"},{"slug":"index-of-industrial-production-iip-8-core-industries","title":"Index of Industrial Production (IIP)- 8 Core Industries"},{"slug":"index-of-industrial-production-iip-overall","title":"Index of Industrial Production (IIP)- Overall"},{"slug":"nifty-50","ti